<title>USA: Indium Corp of America hikes price by $35 a kilo.</title>
<headline>Indium Corp of America hikes price by $35 a kilo.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indium Corp of America said it has raised its posted indium price by $35 to $260 a kilogram or $8.09 a troy ounce, effective March 6.</p>
<p>The company last raised its price by $15 to $225 a kilo on Feb 26.</p>
<p>Traders said on Thursday that prices were moving higher as Japanese consumers rushed to cover in a market largely devoid of good quality material while Western producer stocks were thought to be low.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
